  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Yemen Joint Response 2024-26 (DRA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SC and SF focus on strengthening the resilience of vulnerable households by creating income-generating and agricultural livelihoods to enhance food security in selected districts. Unconditional Cash Transfer (UTC) and Conditional Cash Transfer (CCT) components will be used to meet basic food needs in the lean season and rehabilitate community infrastructures. UCT will target households (HH) who do not have the capacity to work (female, elderly, people with disability). The project&apos;s second focus in the area is on improving the availability of clean water and promoting hygiene practices to reduce malnutrition rates and enhance protection.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save the Children (SC) and Sphereye (SF) will implement a 36 month intervention to meet the immediate needs and strengthen resilience of crisis and conflict affected people in Sa&apos;ada Governorate in the sectors of Food Security &amp; Livelihoods and WASH.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will mainly target boys and girls, youth and women, elderly, people with disabilities, and small holder farmers</narrative>
  </description>
